  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `SetupDef` has a new field `order: Option<u32>`.\n- `CreateSetup` writes the next order: one past the highest stored order, 0 for the first setup.\n- `CreateSetup` refuses creation when the highest stored order is `u32::MAX`. The refusal preserves the document and program order.\n- `setup::setups` sorts by `order`. Setups without an order (older files) sort first, by name. This is the old behaviour for these files.\n- The project file saves `order` on the setup row. `PROJECT_VERSION` steps from 76 to 77 (second review). A v76 file has no `order`; it opens unchanged and keeps name order. A v76 reader refuses a v77 file.\n- `examples/first-continuous-4axis-part.camproj` states version 77. `deburr_chord_width.rs` now pins `>= 76` and the current version, not the literal 76.\n- `add_setup`, `get_job`, `operation_order` and the post all read `setup::setups`. They now all follow the creation order.\n- Comments in `setup.rs` that said \"by name\" now say \"program order\".\n\n## Cause\n\n`setup::setups` returned the setups in name order. `Front_A90` sorted before `Setup1`. Thus it was listed and posted first, although it took its datum and stock from `Setup1`.\n\n## Tests\n\n- New pin `crates/app/tests/setup_creation_order.rs`:\n  - `a_setup_created_second_stays_second_whatever_its_name`: `Setup1`, then `Front_A90` (datum from `Setup1`). The names and the operation order keep the creation order. A third setup goes last. Delete and undo give it back its place.\n  - `the_creation_order_survives_save_and_load_and_reaches_the_post`: save, `open_project` over MCP, `get_job` and `add_setup` list the creation order, and the posted program has `Setup1`'s operation before `Front_A90`'s.\n- Red before the fix: both tests failed (`left: [\"Front_A90\", \"Setup1\"]`).\n- Mutations:\n  - Remove the sort in `setup::setups`: both pins red.\n  - Save writes `order: None` (`wire.rs`): the save/load pin red.\n  - Load reads `order: None` (`apply.rs`): the save/load pin red.\n  - Each restored: green.\n- Changed test `setup_delete_order.rs`: it pinned the old name-order law (its fixture created `B_Middle` last and expected it in the middle by name). The fixture now creates A, B, C in that order. The test still pins that undo of `DeleteSetup` restores the middle place and the posted program.\n- Final head: `e0e87fa1218e5d5964f6657e1d6dca46751c30e1`.\n- Base: `upstream/main` `ef157211438104997fc9e51f7e3affc4db303545`, fetched after upstream advanced during the first gate run.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 60 steps, 0 failed.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: 207 steps, 0 failed, 41.5 minutes. The release build and all app heavy targets passed. The gate handled #1950 and #2849 as expected failures.\n- Heavy lanes: `app heavy: lib`, `bins`, every selected integration target, and `doc`. The setup command change selects every app heavy target.\n- First heavy run against base `148a5c832aa811bab9cae5c7f69e0ad945ee92d4`: 207 steps, 0 failed. Both gates were repeated after the base advanced.\n- `cargo clippy -j 6 -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed on the final head.\n- `cargo test -j 6 -p camcraft-app --test conformance --test golden_cl --test solid_law_goldens`: passed. Counts: 7, 33 and 7.\n- The quick gate ran `app suites: example_catalog`: 37 passed, 4 ignored. It also ran `example_catalog_adaptive`: 1 passed.\n- New pin: `exhausted_setup_order_refuses_creation_without_changing_the_program`. It uses the final available order and loads that project. Creation then refuses without changing the document, setup order or operation order.\n- Pin proof: restore both production files from the reviewed head, then run the new pin. It fails with `exhausted order must refuse creation`. Restore the fix and run `setup_creation_order`: 3 passed.\n- The commands used `RUSTC_WRAPPER=` and `CAMCRAFT_NO_SCCACHE=1`. Gates set `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0`.\n\n## Second review round (head `4df4fc9f7`)\n\n- New pin: `a_v76_file_keeps_name_order_and_a_newer_file_is_refused`. A v76 file with no `order` opens with name order (setups and operations). It saves again with only the version changed. A file one version newer is refused.\n- Pin proof: set `PROJECT_VERSION` back to 76. The pin fails (`setup order needs project v77`). Restore 77: `setup_creation_order` 4 passed, `setup_delete_order` 2 passed.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 62 steps. One step failed on the first run: `deburr_chord_width` pinned the literal 76. After the fix, `--failed` ran that step: passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed.\n- `conformance`: 7 passed. `golden_cl`: 33 passed. `continuous_4axis_part` version test: passed. The quick gate ran `example_catalog` and `example_catalog_adaptive`: passed.\n- Heavy lanes: not run for this round. The second review says heavy lanes are not a condition for this PR (maintainer decision of 2026-11-22, #3556). The reviewer runs the named suites on the trial merge.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nPrograms: none. Project: `examples/first-continuous-4axis-part.camproj` changes only its version line (76 to 77), for the version step. The catalog, conformance, CL golden and solid-law golden suites ran. No `.nc`, `.cl` or `examples/catalog/**` file changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- UI screenshots: no UI files changed. This fix adds a command refusal.\n- The UI setup tree. It reads the same `setup::setups`; no UI test was added.\n- A file saved by this build and opened by a released build. The version step makes a v76 build refuse it (`UnsupportedVersion`); the pin checks the refusal at `PROJECT_VERSION + 1`.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #3251 touches `crates/app/src/project/apply.rs` (`check_and_apply`), a different function. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n- #2924 touches `crates/app/src/schema.rs` (`Sketch` doc comment), a different item. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\n## Follow-up\n\nThe reorder command and its MCP tool are filed as #3484.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/3447-setup-creation-order.md`.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: Setups keep the order in which they were created; a setup added later is listed and posted after earlier setups, whatever its name.\n\nFixes #3447\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n",
